# Applies to builds that use the REPOSITORY ROOT as their context:
#   - apps/web/Dockerfile, which needs the root because @taskboard/web imports
#     three sibling workspaces (packages/app, packages/shared, packages/ui).
#   - services/messaging-svc, services/notification-svc and services/ws-gateway's
#     Dockerfiles, which need the root because their go.mod replaces
#     github.com/task-board/shared-kafkaauth with the sibling module
#     services/shared/kafkaauth.
#   - services/auth-svc, services/task-svc, services/integrations-svc,
#     services/telemetry-svc and services/email-worker's Dockerfiles, which
#     need the root because their requirements.txt references the sibling
#     package services/shared/kafka_security as a local path dependency.
#   - services/auth-svc, services/task-svc, services/integrations-svc and
#     services/telemetry-svc's Dockerfiles ALSO reference the sibling package
#     services/shared/crypto (at-rest column encryption) the same way.
#   - all five (also email-worker) ALSO reference services/shared/tracing
#     (OTel Kafka context-propagation + shutdown helpers) the same way.
#
# Without this file that context is ~1.9 GB: apps/ and services/ each carry their
# own node_modules and build output, and .git is large. Everything these builds
# actually need is a package manifest, a lockfile, or source.
#
# The remaining per-service images (region-bridge, infra/caddy) are UNAFFECTED
# — they build from narrow contexts that never contained any of this.

# ── VCS and editor state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.git_backup
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude

# ── Dependency trees (reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile) ───────
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# ── Build output (rebuilt inside the image; stale copies would shadow it) ───
**/dist
**/out
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/desktop/release
apps/extension/dist.crx
apps/extension/dist.zip

# ── Python / Go artifacts from the service trees ────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/bin

# ── Secrets and key material. These must never enter a build context, even
#    though the web build would not read them — a COPY . in any future
#    root-context Dockerfile would otherwise bake them into a layer.
.env
.env.*
keys/
infra/postgres/certs/*.crt
infra/postgres/certs/*.key
infra/redis/certs/*.crt
infra/redis/certs/*.key
apps/desktop/build/certs
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12

# ── Operational data that is large and never a build input ──────────────────
backups/
.deploy/
.shot/
.ui-verify/
loadtest/
**/*.log

# ── Docs and compose files: not build inputs, and touching them should not
#    invalidate a single cached layer.
*.md
docs/
docker-compose*.yml
Jenkinsfile
Makefile
